{
  "_doc": "The build of each four-legged family (scripts/world3d/animal_build.gd), so every species has its own silhouette and each of its skins (variants in animal_rigs.json) share it. torso: overlapping rounded masses [x, y, z, rx, ry, rz] as shares of the body's half length, half height and half width (x forward): a cow is a barrel with a withers hump and hip bones, a horse has a deep chest, a narrow waist and a round croup. leg: thick (x the family's width), taper (the lower leg's width against the upper), bend (0.5 is dead straight; a little above shows a knee), hoof (cloven, round), stance (how far apart the legs stand, share of the half width). head: skull_at/skull_r and muzzle_at/muzzle_r in the head's own length and height, eye (size against the rig's). Anything left out keeps the old default. body: {box, stations: [[x, top, bottom, width]]} a sculpted body (scripts/world3d/animal_loft.gd) from its side outline, instead of torso masses. head.shape: stations the same way for the head (x in half-lengths of the head). limbs: radius profiles [[t, r]] of the upper and lower leg (t 0 at the body end), and neck.profile likewise (t 0 at the chest). muscles: extra rounded masses [x, y, z, rx, ry, rz] (z mirrored to both sides) that give shoulder and haunch definition. head.len: how long the head is against the rig's head length (0.6 is the old default).",
